a$, and $\\phi$, with $\\ell < 0$ on one side of the throat and $\\ell > 0$ on the other, each point of the plot a sphere of areal radius $a + |\\ell|$. Off the shell the spacetime is Schwarzschild's vacuum, where $K = 12r_s^2/(a + |\\ell|)^6$ and the Ricci scalar $R$ vanishes.","Toward the throat $K$ rises to its greatest value, $12r_s^2/a^6 = 3.146/r_s^4$, the spheres there being the least of the wormhole, and it falls to $0.002036/r_s^4$ at $|\\ell| = 3\\,r_s$, where the areal radius is $4.25\\,r_s$. Far out it falls off as $12r_s^2/\\ell^6$. The two sides are mirror images, and $K$ has a kink at the throat, where its slope jumps from $72r_s^2/a^7$ to minus it, since $r = a + |\\ell|$ has a kink there. The chart has no horizon: $g^{\\ell\\ell} = 1 - r_s/(a + |\\ell|)$ is least $1 - r_s/a = 0.2$ at the throat.","All of the matter is the shell at the throat, where $R$ is the distribution $-2(4a - 3r_s)\\delta(\\ell)/a^2$, which is $-2.56\\,\\delta(\\ell)/r_s$ here, with $\\delta$ the Dirac delta. It is negative at every throat outside the horizon, since $a > r_s$ makes $4a - 3r_s$ positive."],"settings":"$r_s = 1$, the unit of every length, and $a = 1.25\\,r_s$, the throat radius of its other drawings.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_s^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-3}$ to $10$; every value drawn lies within it, and each side's curve stops $10^{-5}\\,r_s$ short of the throat, where the vacuum ends."}]}
